## Mode Gating Contract

- Home mode (`mode === 'home')`:
  - Renders globe stack: `features/home/HomeGlobeView` (uses `features/globe/GlobeScene` and `GlobeController`).
  - Shows `TopHud`, `BottomHud`, `DatasetControllerContainer`, and `ResetGlobeContainer` when globe is ready and not loading.
  - Tooltip handling via `features/ui/TooltipLayer` and `useHoverTooltip`.
- Settings mode (`mode === 'settings')`:
  - `SettingsGearContainer` renders the settings panel inline in the central pane (not full-screen route), maintaining sidebars.
  - Globe and Bottom HUD are hidden.
- Avatar mode (`mode === 'avatar')`:
  - Central pane renders `features/avatar/AvatarRigPanel`.
  - Globe layer and Bottom HUD are hidden to avoid layout conflicts.
  - Sidebars may auto-collapse depending on layout state.

This gating prevents UI overlap (e.g., the Reset Globe button floating over non-globe views) and stabilizes the main composer.

